
  CHasm: everything on this screen is x86_64 assembly, X server included.

  Mod4 is the Super (Windows) key. On a Mac it is Cmd, but Cmd+Q and
  Cmd+W go to the browser. Your own desktop may catch some Mod4 keys too.

    Mod4+?          every key, on one screen
    Mod4+Return     a new terminal
    Mod4+1 .. 0     workspaces
    Mod4+q          close the window
    Mod4+w          next wallpaper
    Alt+t           see-through terminal

  Try  show ~/.tilerc  to read the window manager's whole config.

  More: https://isene.org/chasm/

